-- CAPABILITY --------------- errors/cap_mismatch_2.march

`greet` takes a `Cap(IO.Console)` parameter, but capability values were retired: a function no longer receives its authority, it uses the current authority, which `main`'s `needs` clause asks for and each operation checks. [cap_param_retired]
help: remove the parameter and the argument at each call; to state what `greet` may use, give it a `needs` clause.

7 |   fn greet(con : Cap(IO.Console), name : String) : () do
                     ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^


    fix (`forge fix` applies it):

 7 -   fn greet(con : Cap(IO.Console), name : String) : () do
 7 +   fn greet(name : String) : () do
13 -     greet(cap, "march")
13 +     greet("march")

    run `march --explain cap_param_retired`


-- WARNING: CAPABILITY ------ errors/cap_mismatch_2.march

`main` asks for its authority with `Cap` parameters, which are deprecated and will be removed in the next release: a capability value grants nothing since the current authority replaced it. [deprecated_main_cap]
help: request it with a `needs` clause: `fn main() needs IO do`.

12 |   fn main(cap : Cap(IO)) do
                     ^^^^^^^


    fix (`forge fix` applies it):

12 -   fn main(cap : Cap(IO)) do
12 +   fn main() do
12 -   fn main(cap : Cap(IO)) do
12 +   fn main(cap : Cap(IO)) needs IO do

    run `march --explain deprecated_main_cap`


-- CAPABILITY --------------- errors/cap_mismatch_2.march

`greet` needs console access, but `cap` is the full IO capability. [cap_mismatch]

13 |     greet(cap, "march")
               ^^^

    `IO` contains `IO.Console`, but a capability is never narrowed implicitly.
    help: capability values were retired; remove the parameter and this argument (see the `cap_param_retired` error on the parameter).

    `greet` needs `Cap(IO.Console)`:

13 |     greet(cap, "march")
         ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^

    `cap` was bound here as `Cap(IO)`:

12 |   fn main(cap : Cap(IO)) do
               ^^^



after fix: exit 0
